    "body": "#### What type of PR is this?\r\n/kind feature\r\n/sig scheduling\r\n\r\n### What this PR does / why we need it:\r\nThis PR introduces an optional, analysis‑only feature that quantifies the real influence of scoring plugins on scheduling outcomes. When enabled per profile, the scheduler performs a lightweight leave‑one‑out analysis after scoring to determine whether a plugin changes the winner and how much it affects the top‑K ranking. Results are emitted via logs and new metrics. Scheduling behavior is unchanged. \r\n\r\n#### Config\r\nNew per‑profile config block:\r\nprofiles:\r\n- schedulerName: default-scheduler\r\n   pluginInfluence:\r\n      enabled: true\r\n      samplePercent: 20   \r\n      topK: 5 \r\n\r\n#### Metrics\r\n\r\n- scheduler_plugin_influence_winner_change_total{profile,plugin,changed}\r\n- scheduler_plugin_influence_topk_overlap_ratio{profile,plugin}          \r\n\r\n#### Logging\r\nAt V(4), each analyzed plugin emits:\r\n\r\n- baseline winner\r\n- winner without plugin\r\n- winner changed (bool)\r\n- top‑K overlap count and ratio\r\n\r\n#### Which issue(s) this PR is related to:\r\nFixes issue #136788 . \r\n\r\n#### Special notes for your reviewer:\r\n\r\n#### Does this PR introduce a user-facing change?\r\nAdded a new user-facing scheduler configuration field (pluginInfluence under each profile) that exposes new metrics and logs. Scheduling behavior remains unchanged, but it does add opt‑in observability.\r\n\r\n#### Future Changes\r\nAdd a targeted unit test for this analyzePluginInfluence to assert winner change + top‑K overlap\r\n\r\n\r\nRequesting feedback from @novahe ",
